=== STICKY: Every feature in fo4-ocbpc 1.1.1 ===
[b]Every feature in fo4-ocbpc 1.1.1[/b]
[i]alone[/i] = works with just this DLL; [i]Anatomy[/i] = switched on by Anatomy's config; [i]Rapport[/i] = needs Rapport.
[b]Runtimes[/b]: one DLL for 1.10.163 (F4SE 0.6.23) and the Anniversary Edition 1.11.x (its F4SE), with Runtime Database on every version; tested in game on 1.11.240, on 1.10.163 awaiting players' confirmation, next-gen 1.10.984 untested.

[b]Collision[/b]
[list]
[*]Each collider pushes once per frame, for every OCBPC config ([i]alone[/i]).
[*]A penis collides as one continuous tube with a measured head profile ([i]Anatomy[/i]). Thrust wobble on the real mesh: anus 0.69 → 0.21, vagina 0.26 → 0.13.
[*]Held props are colliders ([i]Anatomy[/i]): what an animation hangs on a hand becomes collision along its length, limited to the bones you name. A mug at the chest pushes nothing; weapons are excluded.
[*]A penis never pushes its own owner.
[/list]
[b]Bones and config[/b]
[list]
[*]Genital bones are created at run time under each actor's pelvis ([i]Anatomy[/i]). No skeleton file is shipped; one that already has them is left alone. Cost: one comparison per skin.
[*]Layered config: your ocbp.ini is read first, then Anatomy's; collision files are appended the same way. Installing Anatomy never overwrites your physics config.
[*]With no ocbp.ini of yours, Anatomy's own default preset stands in, and its collision only with it ([i]Anatomy[/i]).
[*]Anatomy's own bones pass a preset's [Whitelist] (useWhitelist=1 froze the genitals before 1.1.1); the preset's race whitelist still applies ([i]Anatomy[/i]).
[*]Bones on every loaded actor, not only your cell's, put back at rest when OCBPC isn't simulating her ([i]Anatomy[/i]; built, not yet confirmed in game).
[/list]
[b]Aim and shape[/b] ([i]Anatomy[/i], AAF scenes only)
[list]
[*]Needs the men's skeleton from ZeX (Penis_00..05 in one chain); on any other the aim stays off and says so in the log.
[*]Turns toward the opening the animation meant: a new lock turns at most 35°, is kept up to 45°, and an entry is allowed up to 75° off the way in. A short shaft stretches at most 10%.
[*]Bends along a measured canal path; the throat path follows head and neck; a curled hand is a target of its own.
[*]Exact per-frame bend, no lag on a fast pull-out; switching openings crossfades.
[*]A thinner shaft (×0.85) and a bigger head (×1.2 to 1.25, fixed per man), scaled on his bones.
[/list]
[b]The mouth[/b] ([i]Anatomy[/i])
[list]
[*]Opens to what is at the lips, over the animation's own face, and hands back when nothing is there.
[*]Lips fit the cross-section inside: 15 measured morphs solved every frame at 7 points. Corners open around a wide shaft and hug a narrow one. Lips follow at 60/50 per second.
[*]Reads the real width, head included. Brows, cheeks and nose react to contact, depth and speed.
[/list]
[b]Faces[/b] ([i]Rapport[/i])
[list]
[*]Rapport's face is written after the engine's merge, so it can close eyes and a jaw the animation opened ([i]alone[/i] on the engine side). Blinks still work.
[*]Lip sync is kept for exactly the line being spoken; faces ease in and out over 250 ms.
[*]Glances into the partner's eyes for 4-7 s, a face for the glance, and eye rolls (needs Anatomy's [i]glances=1[/i]; eye rolls are built, not yet seen in game).
[*]Brows draw in as oral depth grows.
[/list]
[b]Stability[/b]
[list]
[*]Every address comes from Runtime Database; every hook and every class the engine reads directly is checked first, and whatever doesn't prove out stays off, logged. The game's own functions are never modified.
[*]A fault while installing the eye or mouth hook turns only that feature off.
[*]No DetourXS: every hook goes through F4SE's trampoline; F4SE is never named a plugin (AE kills the game over it); a log a relaunched game cannot wipe; the discovery log for modders is off by default.
[*]Offline test suites, each proven by planted faults: aim (22 cases), face (51 checks), lips (17), tube (8).
[/list]
[b]Not yet confirmed in game:[/b] 1.1.0 on 1.10.163 and next-gen, bones kept outside your cell, toys as one tube, big-toy and fist stretch, Rapport's MCM knobs for the engine, and brows following vaginal and anal depth. Tell us what you see.

=== STICKY: fo4-ocbpc settings, for modders ===
[b]fo4-ocbpc settings, for modders[/b]
Two ini files are read, yours first: [i]Data\F4SE\Plugins\ocbp.ini[/i], then [i]Data\F4SE\Plugins\Anatomy\ocbp.ini[/i]. OCBPCollisionConfig.txt is read the same way and appended. With no ocbp.ini of yours, [i]Anatomy\ocbp-default.ini[/i] stands in, and [i]Anatomy\OCBPCollisionConfig-default.txt[/i] is read only then.

[list]
[*][b][Attach], bone sections, [Override:*], [Whitelist][/b]: OCBPC's physics, as always.
[*][b][Props][/b]: held props as colliders (nodes, radius, spacing, maxLength, minBound, targets). Off unless [i]nodes[/i] is set.
[*][b][Bones][/b]: run-time bones, [i]name=parent,x,y,z[/i] under Pelvis_skin. Only what is listed.
[*][b][Tube][/b]: penis chains, and props with [i]props=1[/i], as one tube; skin, glans, glansProfile. Off unless [i]enabled=1[/i].
[*][b][Aim][/b]: the chain, the openings and their paths, the throat, angles and reach. Off unless [i]enabled=1[/i].
[*][b][Shape][/b]: shaft, headMin, headMax. Off unless [i]enabled=1[/i].
[*][b][Mouth][/b]: the contact mouth, the lip table, corners, glans, face reaction terms. Off unless [i]enabled=1[/i].
[*][b][Face][/b]: authority (Rapport's faces) and react. On by default.
[*][b][Eyes][/b]: the eye hook, on by default; [i]glances=1[/i] tells Rapport glances work (off unless set); uMax, vMin, vMax, rollMax, axes.
[*][b][Log][/b]: [i]discover=1[/i] lists genital- or toy-looking nodes on nearby actors. It walks their scene graphs every 2 s, so it is off unless you set it.
[/list]
Every key's default, clamp and meaning is in the header comment of its source file (Mouth.h, Aim.h, Eyes.h, Bones.h, TubeCollide.h, FaceAuthority.h) and config.cpp, in [url=https://github.com/ReidenXerx/fo4-ocbpc]the repository[/url]. [i]probe=[/i] and [i]test=[/i] keys are for development and log heavily.
